 is read (not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the row is formed). A struct rather than a lazy map, so an algorithm that keeps an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator per vertex on its stack (Tarjan’s) allocates nothing for it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph\/successors","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.Successors","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Successors","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"}}}